From 9c7f6b56e61cfe5257287802374b75607722933d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Simoes <lucassimoe@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:10:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] can: rockchip_canfd: stop the TX queue on bus-off

On bus-off the driver stops the chip and calls can_bus_off(), but
leaves the TX queue running. can_restart() then flushes the echo skbs
"because the device is bus-off and no messages can come in or go out",
and rkcanfd_set_mode() restarts the chip, which resets tx_head and
tx_tail. A frame queued between the flush and the reset gets an echo
slot that is outside the new [tx_tail, tx_head) window. Nothing frees
it again, so every later frame that maps to that slot is dropped and
TX is dead until the module is reloaded:

  rockchip_canfd fea50000.can can0: can_put_echo_skb: BUG! echo_skb 1 is occupied!

This is likely the "TX starvation after repeated Bus-Off" issue listed
in rockchip_canfd.h. On an RK3588 robot whose bus goes bus-off about
once a second it shows up within minutes to hours.

Stop the queue before stopping the chip. rkcanfd_set_mode() already
wakes it after the restart.

---
 drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c b/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
index 938cd5a..cbfc11c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/can/rockchip/rockchip_canfd-core.c
@@ -595,6 +595,11 @@ static int rkcanfd_handle_state_error_int(struct rkcanfd_priv *priv)
 	can_change_state(ndev, cf, tx_state, rx_state);
 
 	if (new_state == CAN_STATE_BUS_OFF) {
+		/* can_restart() flushes the echo skbs assuming nothing is
+		 * sent while bus-off. Keep the queue stopped until
+		 * rkcanfd_set_mode() has restarted the chip.
+		 */
+		netif_stop_queue(ndev);
 		rkcanfd_chip_stop(priv, CAN_STATE_BUS_OFF);
 		can_bus_off(ndev);
 	}
-- 
